WEBVTT

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.200
Storm's coming, and you boys...

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.600
You are smack in the middle of it.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.300
You know the truth about
Sammy and the other children.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.800
Andrew Gallagher. Ava Wilson.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.300
I didn't hurt anybody. Not yet.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.500
Max, your abilities started
seven months ago, right?

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.300
How'd you know that?

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.800
The same thing killed our mothers.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:42.900
You and I were chosen.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.000
For what? I don't know.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.100
I saw this guy die
days before it happened.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.900
You can make people
do things, can't you?

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.900
You can tell them what to think.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.800
Cherry ride. Can I have it? Sure, man.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:01.700
You must be one of us.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.200
Who? The psychics.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.000
Screw you, buddy, 'cause
i'm a secretary from peoria,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:06.800
And i'm not part of anything.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.200
This demon tells me they have soldiers

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.600
To fight in this coming war

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.600
Psychics fighting on hell's side.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.500
The yellow-Eyed man tells me
to do things -- Awful things.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.300
He told me he's got big plans.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.100
Maybe this is his plan. Maybe
we're all supposed to be --

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.500
What, killers? Give me a break.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.900
No one's heard anything about Ava.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.800
She's just -- Into
thin air, you know?

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.800
Sulfur. Ava.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.800
Demon's been here.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.900
If something bad's
coming, it's coming fast,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.400
And their side holds all the cards.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.400
We can't run from this,
and you can't protect me.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.200
Damn it, Sam, this whole thing
is spinning out of control.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.100
Hey, don't forget the
extra onions this time, huh?

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.900
Dude, i'm the one who's
gonna have to ride in the car

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.000
With your extra onions.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.300
Hey, see if they got any pie.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.400
Bring me some pie!

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.400
Bring me some pie.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.600
Sam?

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.800
Sulfur

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.200
Sam!

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.200
Sammy!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.600
Sam!

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.500
Sammy!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.800
Sam!

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.800
Andy? Sam.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.500
What are you doing here? I don't know.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.000
What am I doing here? I don't know.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.600
Where are we?

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.900
Andy, look, calm down.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:16.500
I can't calm down.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.800
I just woke up in
freaking frontier land.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.000
What's the last thing you remember?

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.600
Honestly, my fourth bong load.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.100
It was weird.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:30.900
All of a sudden,

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.600
There was this really
intense smell, like a...

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.300
Like sulfur?

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:37.900
How did you know that?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.200
Dean.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.500
Your brother -- Is
he -- Is he here?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.600
I don't know where he is.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.400
I don't know if he's...

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.100
Hello?

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.300
Woman: no! Help me!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.500
Okay, okay, i'm here.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.500
We're gonna get you out, all right?

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:01.900
Just hold on a second.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.800
All right, one second.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:17.100
Ava? Oh, my god! Sam!

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.000
Hey.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:20.800
So, I guess you guys know each other.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:22.900
Yeah.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.000
How did you -- I
mean, how did --

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.200
Ava, have you been here this whole time?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.500
What whole time? I just woke
up in there a half an hour ago.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.000
Well, you've been gone for five months.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.800
My brother and I have been
looking for you everywhere.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.800
That's impossible 'cause
I saw you two days ago.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.200
You didn't. I'm sorry.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.500
But that makes no sense. It's...not...

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.300
Oh, my god! My fianc? Brady.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.200
If I've been missing for that
long, he must be freaking out!

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.000
Well...

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:52.900
Oh!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:55.600
Hey.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.200
Andy -- Also
freaking out.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.200
Okay.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.700
What's happening?

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.100
Well, I, uh...

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.500
I don't really know yet,
but I know one thing.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.600
I know what the three
of us have in common.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.900
Man: hello? Anybody there?

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.700
Maybe more than three.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.600
Wait.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:19.800
Hello?

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.000
Hey!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.400
Hey, you guys all right?

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.200
Think so.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.300
I'm Sam.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.400
I'm Jake. Lily.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:29.700
Are there any more of you?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.900
No.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:31.900
How did we even get here?

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.500
A minute ago, I was in san diego.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.200
Well, if it makes you feel any better,

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.900
I went to sleep last
night in Afghanistan.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.500
Let me take a wild guess.
You two are both 23?

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:45.700
We all are, and we all have abilities.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:46.800
What?

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.500
It started a little over a year ago.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.300
You find you can do things
you didn't think were possible.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.500
I have visions. I see
things before they happen.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.600
Yeah, me too.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.900
And I can put thoughts into people's
heads -- Like, make them do stuff.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.300
Oh, but don't worry. I don't
think it works on you guys.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.900
Oh, but get this -- Um,
I've been practicing,

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.300
Training my brain,
like meditation, right?

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:10.600
So now it's not just
thoughts that I can beam out,

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.900
But images, too --
Like, anything I want.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.700
It's like bam! People, they see it.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.300
This one guy I know -- Total
dick -- I used it on him.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.300
Gay porn all hours of the day.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.200
It's just like...

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.100
You should have seen
the look on his face.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.700
You go, "simon says give me
your wallet," and they do?

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.400
You have visions? That's great.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.000
I'd kill for something like that.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.700
Lily, listen, it's okay.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.700
No, it's not.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:50.100
I touch people. Their hearts stop.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.500
I can barely leave my house.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.400
My life's not exactly improved.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.100
So screw you. I just want to go home.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.200
And we don't?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.800
Don't -- Hey,
gs, come on.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.100
Look, whether we like it
or not, we're all here,

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:05.000
And so we all have to deal with this.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.800
Who brought us h here?

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.600
It's less of a "who."
It's more of a "what."

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.100
What does that mean?

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.400
It's, uh...

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.300
It's a demon.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.900
This is it -- All demonic signs
and omens over the past month.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.400
Are you joking? There's nothing here.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:31.600
Exactly.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.800
Come on, there's got to be something.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:35.600
What about the normal,
low-Level stuff --

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:36.900
You know, exorcisms, that kind of thing?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.100
There's nothing. It's completely quiet.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:43.300
How are we supposed to look for
Sam, close our eyes and point?

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:49.200
Sam: Ash, what do you got?

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:52.200
Okay, listen. It's a
bit negatory on Sam.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.100
Come on, man. You got
to give us something.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.000
We're looking at a
3,000-Mile haystack here.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.800
Listen, Dean. I did find something.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:01.100
Well, what?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.800
I can't talk over this line, Dean.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.300
Come on, I don't have time for this.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.400
Make time, ok, cause this..

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.800
What's up? What's going on?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.300
Not only does this

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.000
Almost definitely help you
find your brother, this is...

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:17.900
It's huge.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.700
So get here now.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:25.900
I guess we're going to the roadhouse.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:27.300
Come on.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.200
So, we're soldiers in a demon
war to bring on the apocalypse?

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.000
When you put
it like that --

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.500
And we've been picked? Why us?

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.600
I'm not sure, okay?
But look, I just know --

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.600
Sam. I'm sorry.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.200
Psychics and spoon-Bending
is one thing, but demons?

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.600
It sounds crazy. It
doesn't just sound it.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.800
I don't care what you think.

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:54.100
If we're gathered here together,
that means it's starting.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.700
The only thing I got to do is
stay away from wackjobs, okay?

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.700
I've heard enough. I'm
better off on my own.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.400
Fyi -- So
are you.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:04.900
Jake, hold on.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.500
Jake!

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.200
Hello?

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:47.200
It's all right. Don't be scared.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:50.600
Are you lost?

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:54.500
Hello?

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.300
Get back!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:26.500
Just so you know...

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.100
That was a demon.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.500
And that thing?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.700
I'm not sure, but I
think it was an achiri --

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.400
A demon that disguises
itself as a little girl.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.200
Still doesn't tell us where we are.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:45.700
Andy, you with me or what?

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:47.200
Give me a minute.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.200
I'm still working
through "demons are real."

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:56.900
I've seen that bell before.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.000
I think I know
where we are now --

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.300
Cold oak, south dakota.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.400
The town's so haunted,
every single resident fled.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:09.700
Swell. Good to know we're
somewhere so historical.

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:12.800
Why in the world would that
demon or whatever put us here?

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.400
I'm wondering the same thing.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:18.500
You know what? It doesn't matter.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.700
The only sane thing to do here
is get the hell out of dodge.

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.200
Wait, hold on.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.300
Lily, the only way out
is through miles of woods.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.400
Beats hanging out with demons.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.500
Lily, we don't know what's going on yet.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.900
We don't even know how
many of them are out there.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.300
Yeah, he's right.
We should --

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.100
Don't say "we." I'm not part of "we."

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.900
I have nothing in
common with any of you.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.200
Okay, look.
I know --

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.300
You don't know anything.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.200
I
to--

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.600
I accidentally touched my girlfriend.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:52.400
I'm sorry.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.600
Whatever.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.200
I feel like i'm in a nightmare,

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.400
And it just keeps
getting worse and worse.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.100
I've lost people, too.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.300
I have a brother out there right now.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.700
He could be dead, for all I know.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:16.800
We're all in bad shape,
but i'm telling you,

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:19.400
The best way out of this
is to stick together.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:23.000
Fine.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:30.300
We're looking for iron, silver,
salt -- Any kind of weapon.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:31.700
Salt is a weapon?

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.800
It's a brave, new world.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.300
Hopefully, there's food in your world,

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.500
'Cause i'm freaking starving.

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:12.000
What the hell?

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:40.400
My god.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:43.200
You see Ellen?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.000
No.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.300
No Ash, either.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.300
Oh, Ash, damn it!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.000
Hey, you all right?

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:02.600
Yeah, i'm just...

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:04.900
I don't know --
A little dizzy.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.600
A-Are you sure it's
not some kind --

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.300
What, some kind of freaky vision thing?

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.800
No, more like I'd just
kill for a sandwich.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:14.900
I haven't eaten since...

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.400
Well, who knows.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:19.500
No,
it's --

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.800
Don't worry, i'm fine,

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.700
Except for every single
thing that's happening.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.700
You guys, I found something!

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.000
Salt.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.700
That's great, Andy.
Now we all can s--

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:41.600
Where's Lily?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.500
Lily?

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:47.700
Lily!

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:01.500
Oh, my god!

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:12.800
Okay, that -- That's
officially just...

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:14.900
Sam, she's dead! She's dead!

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.800
You said we were chosen for a reason.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:20.500
That is not chosen. That's...killed.

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:22.200
Okay, you know, we
have to get out of here.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.600
I second that emotion.
Not sure that's an option.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.500
Lily was trying to leave.

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:28.400
The demon's not gonna
let us get away that easy.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.600
We got to gear up for the next attack.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.000
Oh, gear up? Yeah.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.800
Okay, well, i'm not a
soldier. I can't do that!

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:37.700
Look, if you want to stay
alive, you're gonna have to.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:44.800
Let's go.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:45.800
Oh, okay.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:47.800
I'll get her down.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.300
You know...

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.300
I was just thinking about how
much Dean would help right now.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:57.800
I'd give my arm for a working phone.

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:00.400
You know, you may not need one.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.200
I, uh, I mean, I've never
tried it long-Distance before.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.100
Do you have anything of Dean's on you,

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.100
Like something he touched?

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:07.400
Uh...

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.300
I got a receipt. Will that work?

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:12.100
Yeah.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.600
D. Hasselhoff?

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.300
Yeah, that's Dean's signature.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:20.500
It...

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.100
It's hard to explain.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:24.200
All right.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:28.300
This is...

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.100
What the hell did Ash know?

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:34.200
We got no way of knowing where
Ellen is or if she's even alive.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:36.200
We got no clue what
Ash was gonna tell us.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:37.500
Now, how the hell are we gonna find Sam?

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.300
We'll find him.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:42.400
Dean? No!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:44.100
Unh!

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.400
Unh!

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:53.000
What was that?

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:57.900
I don't know. Headache?

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.000
You get headaches like that a lot?

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.300
No.

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:06.300
It must be the stress.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:11.700
I could have swore I saw something.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:14.000
What do you mean?
Like -- Like a vision?

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.400
Like what Sam gets? What? No.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:17.500
I'm just saying.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.600
Come on, i'm not some psychic.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.700
Unh! Oh, god! Dean?!

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:28.800
Dean?

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:31.300
Are you with me?

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.400
Yeah, I think so.

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:38.100
I saw Sam. I saw him, Bobby.

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:39.600
It was a vision.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:40.600
Yeah.

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:43.700
I don't know how,
but -- But yeah.

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.100
Whew!

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:48.000
That was about as fun as
getting kicked in the jewels.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:49.100
What else did you see?

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.600
Uh, there was a bell.

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:53.600
What kind of bell?

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.100
Um, like,
a big --

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:00.600
A big bell with some
kind of engraving on it.

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:01.200
I don't know.

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:02.000
Engraving?

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.100
Yeah.

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:05.200
Was it a tree --
Like, an oak tree?

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:07.900
Yeah, exactly.

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:10.900
I know where Sam is.

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:31.700
I-I'm not superman or anything.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:32.700
It's no big deal.

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:34.800
You were in afghanistan
when this started?

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.400
I started getting headaches,

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.400
Then, uh, there was this accident.

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:42.600
This guy flipped his
vehicle on a bad road,

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.000
Got pinned underneath.

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.200
I lifted it off him like it was nothing.

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.400
E-Everybody said it was
a fluke adrenaline thing.

00:22:51.400 --> 00:22:52.700
But then you did it again, right?

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:55.600
Bench-Press 800
pounds, stone-Cold calm.

00:22:57.200 --> 00:22:58.500
I never told anybody, of course.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:22:59.900
It's just too crazy.

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:03.200
Yeah, well, crazy's relative.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:05.100
I'm starting to get that.

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:07.200
Yeah.

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:11.600
By the way, I, uh,
appreciate what you're doing.

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:13.600
What am I doing?

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:16.700
Keeping calm, keeping them calm,

00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:19.100
Especially considering how
freaked to hell you really are.

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:24.600
I've been in some deep
crap before myself.

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:25.600
I know the look.

00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:33.900
Want to know the truth?

00:23:34.900 --> 00:23:36.200
I got this brother, right?

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.300
And he's always telling me how
he's gonna watch out for me,

00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:41.800
How everything's gonna be okay,
like I've been telling them.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:43.100
Yeah.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:45.800
I don't know if I believe it this time.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:49.100
I mean, the size
of what's coming --

00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:52.600
It's bigger than anyone's ever seen.

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:56.700
I mean, it's gonna get bad,
and I-I don't know if --

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:57.800
If we're gonna make it.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:00.700
It doesn't matter if we believe it.

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:02.900
Only matters that they do.

00:24:34.100 --> 00:24:36.200
My horoscope said I shouldn't
have gotten out of bed.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:41.700
How you doing?

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:43.300
Holding up?

00:24:43.300 --> 00:24:44.100
I'm okay.

00:24:45.600 --> 00:24:46.600
What about you?

00:24:46.900 --> 00:24:48.100
Not so okay.

00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:51.600
Why us, Sam?

00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:54.700
What did we do to deserve this?

00:24:55.200 --> 00:24:56.400
Just lucky, I guess.

00:24:56.900 --> 00:24:59.700
If it wasn't for bad luck,
wouldn't have no luck at all.

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:03.800
Just can't wait for this all to be over

00:25:03.800 --> 00:25:06.400
So I can just pretend it never happened.

00:25:08.400 --> 00:25:11.300
Just want to curl up with
Brady and watch bad tv.

00:25:15.300 --> 00:25:16.200
What is it?

00:25:18.800 --> 00:25:20.600
Sam, do you

00:25:22.900 --> 00:25:24.200
Know something that I don't?

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:27.000
Look, Ava.

00:25:30.700 --> 00:25:32.800
I'm sorry. I wish I didn't
have to tell you this

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:33.100
Tell me what?

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:38.600
When the demon broke in
to your house to take you,

00:25:41.300 --> 00:25:42.400
Your fianc?Didn't make it

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:44.900
I'm sorry.

00:25:47.700 --> 00:25:49.600
No, it's...

00:26:26.500 --> 00:26:27.600
Jake, behind you!

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:28.800
Howdy, Sam.

00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:34.200
I'm dreaming.

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:38.700
What do you say you and
I take a little walk?

00:26:48.700 --> 00:26:52.100
You're awfully quiet, Sam.
You're not mad at me, are you?

00:26:53.600 --> 00:26:55.800
I'm gonna tear you to shreds, I swear.

00:26:56.300 --> 00:26:59.200
When you wake up, tiger,
you give it your best shot.

00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:01.100
Where's my brother?

00:27:01.100 --> 00:27:04.700
Quit worrying about Dean.
I'd worry more about yourself.

00:27:04.700 --> 00:27:06.200
What, you gonna kill me?

00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:10.800
I'm trying to help you.
That's why we're talking.

00:27:10.800 --> 00:27:12.400
You're the one i'm rooting for.

00:27:15.300 --> 00:27:16.400
What's that supposed to mean?

00:27:16.900 --> 00:27:19.500
Welcome to the miss america pageant.

00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:21.400
Why do you think you're here?

00:27:21.400 --> 00:27:22.900
This is a competition.

00:27:22.900 --> 00:27:27.100
Only one of you crazy kids is

00:27:27.100 --> 00:27:28.900
Gonna make it out of here alive.

00:27:28.900 --> 00:27:29.800
I thought we were
supposed to be --

00:27:29.800 --> 00:27:31.300
Soldiers in a coming war?

00:27:31.300 --> 00:27:34.800
That's true. You are.
But here's the thing.

00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:38.400
I don't need soldiers.

00:27:40.900 --> 00:27:44.800
I need soldier. I just need the one.

00:27:45.800 --> 00:27:46.300
Why?

00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:48.600
I couldn't just come out
and say that, could I, Sam?

00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:51.200
I had to let everyone think
they had a fighting chance.

00:27:51.200 --> 00:27:52.400
But what I need...

00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:54.700
Is a leader.

00:27:55.400 --> 00:27:56.500
To lead who?

00:27:58.800 --> 00:28:04.000
Oh, I've already got my army
-- Or I will soon, anyway.

00:28:04.400 --> 00:28:05.600
You son of a bitch.

00:28:05.600 --> 00:28:09.300
Honestly, i'm surprised
you hadn't guessed.

00:28:09.300 --> 00:28:12.400
I mean, why do you think so many
children flamed out already --

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:15.600
Max Miller and Andy's
brother -- What's his name?

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:18.700
They weren't strong enough.

00:28:19.300 --> 00:28:25.300
I'm looking for the best and
brightest of your generation.

00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:27.700
My generation?

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:30.300
Well, there's other generations,

00:28:30.300 --> 00:28:31.900
But let's just worry about yours.

00:28:32.300 --> 00:28:33.800
That's why i'm here, Sam.

00:28:33.800 --> 00:28:36.000
I want to give you the inside track.

00:28:36.600 --> 00:28:40.000
You're tough, you're
smart, you're well-Trained,

00:28:40.500 --> 00:28:41.500
Thanks to your daddy.

00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:43.000
Sam.

00:28:45.400 --> 00:28:46.300
Sammy...

00:28:47.700 --> 00:28:48.800
You're my favorite.

00:28:49.400 --> 00:28:54.000
You ruined my life. You
killed everyone I love.

00:28:54.500 --> 00:28:56.700
The cost of doing business, i'm afraid.

00:28:57.800 --> 00:29:00.900
I mean, sweet, little jessica...

00:29:01.600 --> 00:29:03.000
She just had to die.

00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:07.100
You were all set to marry
that little, blond thing,

00:29:07.400 --> 00:29:10.100
Become a tax lawyer with
two kids, a beer gut,

00:29:10.100 --> 00:29:11.800
And a little mcmansion in the suburbs.

00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:14.100
I needed you sharp, on the road,

00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:17.900
Honing your skills
-- Your gifts.

00:29:18.300 --> 00:29:19.300
What about my mom?

00:29:20.300 --> 00:29:21.200
That was bad luck.

00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:22.300
Bad luck.

00:29:22.300 --> 00:29:25.400
She walked
in on us --

00:29:25.900 --> 00:29:27.200
Wrong place, wrong time.

00:29:27.800 --> 00:29:28.500
What does that mean?

00:29:28.500 --> 00:29:31.500
It wasn't about her. It was about you.

00:29:32.400 --> 00:29:33.900
It's always been about you.

00:29:35.400 --> 00:29:36.400
What?

00:29:41.200 --> 00:29:42.100
Well...

00:29:43.700 --> 00:29:47.700
Okay, you caught me
in a charitable mood.

00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:49.300
I'll show you.

00:29:51.600 --> 00:29:53.300
Look familiar? It should.

00:29:57.900 --> 00:30:01.000
Relax, Sam. This is just
a high-Def instant replay.

00:30:01.700 --> 00:30:02.700
Enjoy the show.

00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:04.400
John.

00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:05.200
Mom.

00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:06.200
Is he hungry?

00:30:08.400 --> 00:30:09.300
Shh.

00:30:10.700 --> 00:30:11.600
Okay.

00:30:11.600 --> 00:30:12.600
Wait, mom.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:14.300
Mom!

00:30:14.300 --> 00:30:16.200
What did I just tell you,
Sam? She can't hear you.

00:30:16.800 --> 00:30:17.900
This isn't real.

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:24.400
What the hell are you doing to me?

00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:25.900
Better than mother's milk.

00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:32.600
Does this mean I have...

00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:34.200
Demon blood in me?

00:30:36.500 --> 00:30:37.600
Answer me!

00:30:40.900 --> 00:30:41.600
It's you.

00:30:41.900 --> 00:30:42.800
She knew you.

00:30:46.800 --> 00:30:47.600
No.

00:30:52.800 --> 00:30:53.900
No!

00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:57.600
I don't think you want
to see the rest of this.

00:30:58.900 --> 00:30:59.900
Sam, wake up.

00:31:01.900 --> 00:31:02.900
Ava's missing.

00:31:17.300 --> 00:31:18.600
I'll take the barn and the hotel.

00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:20.400
You take the houses. All right.

00:31:20.800 --> 00:31:21.900
Meet back here in 10 minutes, okay?

00:31:53.700 --> 00:31:55.700
Ava, where'd you go?

00:31:57.200 --> 00:31:58.600
Didn't you hear us yelling?

00:31:58.600 --> 00:31:59.500
Yeah, I heard you.

00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:13.400
What are you doing?

00:32:19.300 --> 00:32:20.100
Holy...

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:23.300
Ah! Aah!

00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:24.800
Aah!

00:32:47.400 --> 00:32:50.200
Sam, I just found him like this!

00:32:50.600 --> 00:32:51.500
What happened?

00:32:51.900 --> 00:32:52.600
I don't know.

00:32:53.300 --> 00:32:54.300
How did that thing get in?

00:33:00.700 --> 00:33:01.500
Where were you?

00:33:01.800 --> 00:33:04.200
I just went to get some
water from the well.

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:06.600
I was only gone, maybe,
like, two minutes.

00:33:08.800 --> 00:33:10.100
You shouldn't have gone outside.

00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:11.900
Ava, we have to stay in here.

00:33:15.700 --> 00:33:16.600
Who did that?

00:33:17.500 --> 00:33:18.700
I don't know.
Maybe Andy --

00:33:18.700 --> 00:33:19.800
Andy wouldn't do that.

00:33:21.700 --> 00:33:23.300
Ava, that line wasn't
broken when I left.

00:33:26.600 --> 00:33:27.300
Ava.

00:33:27.300 --> 00:33:28.300
What? You
don't think --

00:33:28.300 --> 00:33:30.400
I'll tell you what I think. Five months.

00:33:30.900 --> 00:33:33.200
You're the only one with all
that time you can't account for.

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:35.100
And that headache you got...

00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:38.200
Right when the demon got Lily.

00:33:38.200 --> 00:33:39.600
What are you trying to say?

00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:40.500
What happened to you?

00:33:40.500 --> 00:33:41.500
Nothing!

00:33:52.700 --> 00:33:54.100
Had you going, though, didn't I?

00:33:57.100 --> 00:33:58.100
Yeah.

00:33:59.600 --> 00:34:03.000
I've been here a long
time, and not alone, either.

00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:07.500
People just keep showing
up -- Children, like us.

00:34:10.600 --> 00:34:12.500
Batches of three or four at a time.

00:34:12.500 --> 00:34:14.700
You killed them
-- All of them?

00:34:16.700 --> 00:34:18.600
I'm the undefeated heavyweight champ.

00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:19.900
Oh, my god.

00:34:20.200 --> 00:34:22.300
I don't think god has
much to do with this, Sam.

00:34:23.500 --> 00:34:24.400
How could you?

00:34:26.100 --> 00:34:27.700
I had no choice.

00:34:28.400 --> 00:34:29.500
It's me or them.

00:34:29.500 --> 00:34:31.900
After a while, it was easy.

00:34:32.400 --> 00:34:33.600
It was even kind of fun.

00:34:35.500 --> 00:34:36.600
I just stopped fighting it.

00:34:36.900 --> 00:34:37.700
Fighting what?

00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:39.500
Who we are, Sam.

00:34:40.400 --> 00:34:42.100
If you'd just quit your hand-Wringing

00:34:42.100 --> 00:34:43.300
And open yourself up,

00:34:43.300 --> 00:34:45.400
You have no idea what you can do.

00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:47.600
The learning curve is so fast.

00:34:47.600 --> 00:34:51.000
It's crazy, the switches
that just flip in your brain.

00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:55.500
I can't believe I started
out just having dreams.

00:34:58.000 --> 00:34:59.300
Do you know what I can do now?

00:35:00.100 --> 00:35:01.000
Control demons.

00:35:01.700 --> 00:35:04.100
Ah. You are quick on the draw.

00:35:10.100 --> 00:35:11.700
Yeah, i'm sorry, Sam, but...

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:14.000
It's over.

00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:45.300
It looks like the rest
of the way's on foot.

00:35:52.200 --> 00:35:53.000
Let's go.

00:35:58.000 --> 00:35:59.100
I think we can make it out of here now.

00:35:59.700 --> 00:36:00.300
But the achiri demon.

00:36:00.300 --> 00:36:02.200
No, no, no, Ava was
summoning it, controlling it.

00:36:02.200 --> 00:36:03.500
It shouldn't come back
now that she's dead.

00:36:04.100 --> 00:36:05.000
We got to go.

00:36:06.100 --> 00:36:06.800
No. Not "we," Sam.

00:36:08.600 --> 00:36:10.600
Only one of us is getting
out of here. I'm sorry.

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:12.400
What? I had a vision.

00:36:12.400 --> 00:36:14.200
That yellow-Eyed demon,
or whatever it was,

00:36:14.200 --> 00:36:15.100
He talked to me.

00:36:15.100 --> 00:36:16.200
He told me how it was.

00:36:16.200 --> 00:36:17.800
No, Jake, listen. You
can't listen to him.

00:36:17.800 --> 00:36:20.100
Sam, he's not letting us go.

00:36:20.100 --> 00:36:21.000
Only one.

00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:23.100
Now, we don't play
along, he'll kill us both.

00:36:23.900 --> 00:36:26.600
Now, I-I like you, man. I
do, but do the math, here.

00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:28.500
What good's it do for both of us to die?

00:36:29.000 --> 00:36:30.500
Now, I can get out of here,

00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:32.700
I get close to the demon,
I can kill the bastard.

00:36:32.700 --> 00:36:34.100
Come with me. We can kill him together.

00:36:34.100 --> 00:36:35.500
How do I know you won't turn on me?

00:36:36.200 --> 00:36:37.100
I won't.

00:36:37.100 --> 00:36:38.100
I don't know that.

00:36:41.300 --> 00:36:42.100
Okay, look.

00:36:55.800 --> 00:36:56.800
Just come with me, Jake.

00:36:58.200 --> 00:36:59.200
Don't do this.

00:36:59.800 --> 00:37:01.000
Don't play into what it wants.

00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:17.400
Okay.

00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:21.000
Ugh!

00:38:42.900 --> 00:38:43.900
Sam!

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:54.600
Sam!

00:38:54.900 --> 00:38:55.800
Dean.

00:38:58.000 --> 00:38:59.100
Sam, look out!

00:39:01.500 --> 00:39:02.300
No!

00:39:13.300 --> 00:39:14.000
No. Sam.

00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:16.600
Whoa, Sam. Sam.

00:39:16.600 --> 00:39:17.400
Sam, hey.

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:20.700
Hey, come here.

00:39:20.700 --> 00:39:21.300
Let me look at you.

00:39:25.500 --> 00:39:27.600
Hey, look. Look at me.
It's not even that bad.

00:39:28.100 --> 00:39:29.200
It's not even that bad, all right?

00:39:30.700 --> 00:39:31.500
Sammy?

00:39:31.900 --> 00:39:32.600
Sam!

00:39:32.600 --> 00:39:34.900
Hey, listen to me. We're
gonna patch you up, okay?

00:39:35.800 --> 00:39:36.600
You'll be good as new.

00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:38.400
Huh?

00:39:38.600 --> 00:39:39.500
I'm gonna take care of you.

00:39:39.500 --> 00:39:41.700
I got you. That's my job, right?

00:39:41.700 --> 00:39:44.300
Watch out for my
pain-In-The-Ass little brother.

00:39:45.600 --> 00:39:46.500
Sam?

00:39:47.200 --> 00:39:48.100
Sam.

00:39:48.100 --> 00:39:49.000
Sam!

00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:50.700
Sammy!

00:39:55.400 --> 00:39:57.100
No. No, no, no.

00:39:58.200 --> 00:39:59.000
Oh, god.

00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:03.400
Oh, god.

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.100
Sam!



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
